# Agent Conventions

## Architecture

- All agents extend `BaseAgent`; entry point is `run(context) -> AgentResponse`.
- System prompts live in `src/research_agent/prompts/<name>.yaml` (`system` key).
- LLM access only via `LLMProvider` — inject `MockLLMProvider` in tests.

## Critic rules (product)

- `support_score` is 1–9 only; `normalize_score` clamps 10 → 9.
- Score &lt; 7 must have non-empty `score_reason`.
- Honest when no objections (`honesty_note`), do not fabricate flaws.

## Orchestrator

- Paper analysis: `asyncio.gather` on Analyst + Critic via `asyncio.to_thread`.
- Aggregate with explicit `consensus` and `conflicts` lists in `AggregatedAnalysis`.

## LLM output

- Prompts require JSON-only replies. Parse them via a typed Pydantic v2
  model from `research_agent.agents.schemas`, using `parse_model(raw, Model)`.
  Each agent owns one (or a few) schema in that module.
- New schemas should: set `extra="ignore"`, default every field, and use
  `mode="before"` `field_validator`s to coerce wrong-type lists / clamp
  numeric ranges. This preserves the project's "tolerant parser" contract.
- `parse_model` raises `ValueError` (Pydantic `ValidationError` is a
  `ValueError` subclass) on both JSON-decode and schema-validation
  failures — callers either propagate it (paper analysis path) or catch
  it for a graceful fallback (Scribe / Searcher / Illustrator paths).
- Need the raw JSON envelope for an unusual case (e.g. detecting which
  keys the LLM emitted)? Use `schemas.strip_to_json()` directly. Do not
  reinstate `extract_json`.
